Stealth-by-design override: navigator.webdriver must be false under Camoufox.

Stock Firefox under Playwright sets navigator.webdriver=true; Camoufox's
whole purpose is to spoof it to false. Upstream's "has navigator.webdriver
set to true" pins the stock-firefox expectation, so we rewrite the title +
assertion to match Camoufox's surface. Applied unconditionally by setup.sh
after each upstream clone — this turns what would otherwise be a
known-failures deselect into a real green assertion.

If a future upstream release moves the test, edit this patch and bump the
v<TAG>/ directory accordingly. Diff is anchored on the test title so it
survives small surrounding-line drift.

--- a/tests/page/page-basic.spec.ts
+++ b/tests/page/page-basic.spec.ts
@@ -180,8 +180,8 @@
   expect(await frame.evaluate(() => document.querySelector('textarea').value)).toBe('a');
 });

-it('has navigator.webdriver set to true', async ({ page }) => {
-  expect(await page.evaluate(() => navigator.webdriver)).toBe(true);
+it('has navigator.webdriver set to false (camoufox stealth)', async ({ page }) => {
+  expect(await page.evaluate(() => navigator.webdriver)).toBe(false);
 });

